     "text": "HALE LLC MEDICAL GROUP - SUMMARY\n\nPatient: John Carroll \nDOB: 01/31/1977 \nSex: M \nMRN: 995587\n\n---\n\n**Admit Date:** 05/22/2005 \n**Discharge Date:** 02/17/2026 \n**Attending Physician:** Dr. Victoria Morris, Neurology\n\n---\n\n**Principal Diagnosis:** Transient Ischemic Attack (TIA) - Controlled for 21 years\n\n**Secondary Diagnosis:** None\n\n---\n\n**Hospital Course:**\n\nMr. John Carroll, a 49-year-old male, was admitted on 02/17/2026 for evaluation of an upper respiratory infection (URI). He has a significant past medical history of a TIA which occurred 21 years ago, on 05/22/2005, and has been controlled since then.\n\nUpon admission, the patient reported symptoms consistent with a URI, including nasal congestion, sore throat, and a mild cough. There were no neurological symptoms or signs of of TIA. His vital signs were stable with a blood pressure of 127/67 mmHg and a weight of 190 pounds. Physical examination was unremarkable except for findings consistent with an URI. \n\nDuring his hospital stay, Mr. Carroll was monitored for any neurological changes, and none were noted. His URI symptoms were managed with supportive care, including hydration and rest. He did not require any specific antimicrobial therapy as his symptoms were mild and self-limiting.\n\n**Procedures:**\n\n- None performed during this admission.\n\n**Discharge Medications:**\n\n- None specific to TIA as it is controlled. Patient was advised to continue with any routine medications he may be taking for other conditions, though none were documented during this admission.\n\n**Social History:**\n\n- **Tobacco Use:** Former smoker of cigarettes, 1/2 pack per day. Quit on 03/17/2025. Patient minimized his smoking history initially.\n- **Alcohol Use:** None.\n- **Family History:** Mother has Alzheimer's disease, onset at age 71, currently living.\n\n**Follow-Up:**\n\nMr. Carroll was discharged home in stable condition on 02/17/2026. He was advised to follow up with his primary care physician within one week for a post-discharge evaluation. He was also encouraged to maintain a healthy lifestyle, including regular physical activity, a balanced diet, and avoidance of tobacco and excessive alcohol consumption.\n\n**Previous Visits Summary:**\n\n- **02/17/2026:** URI - BP 127/67, Weight 190 lbs\n- **10/02/2025:** Rash - BP 123/61, Weight 183 lbs\n- **05/16/2025:** TIA follow-up - BP 136/62, Weight 195 lbs\n- **12/28/2024:** Back strain - BP 128/62, Weight 197 lbs\n- **08/12/2024:** Ankle sprain - BP 124/72, Weight 191 lbs\n- **03/26/2024:** TIA follow-up - BP 126/66, Weight 195 lbs\n- **11/08/2023:** TIA fo"
